# "quarantine restore" and editable by hand, so an overruled verdict stays overruled.
KEEP_FILE="${KEEP_FILE:-$AUDIT_DIR/keep.txt}"
# Repos and identities a human has judged, one per line, blank lines and #-comments ignored. A
# repo id is pruned wherever it turns up and blocked before it arrives. An identity
# (did:key:z6Mk...) is blocked as a peer, and every repo it is a delegate of is pruned. No
# evidence, age or seed count is asked for, since the verdict is a person's. Pins, our own and
# private repos, and keep.txt still win, since each is a person's word too.
DENY_FILE="$AUDIT_DIR/deny.txt"
# Files a denied repo carried, so copies elsewhere are pruned too. One per line, separated by
# whitespace: git object id, size or -, source (one word, a repo id when it is one), a date;
# #-comments ignored. A row whose source is in keep.txt is ignored, since restoring a repo
# takes its verdict back.
DENY_FILES="$AUDIT_DIR/deny-files.tsv"
# A copy holds at least COPY_MIN_BYTES of those files on its delegates' branches and tags,
# history included, making up at least COPY_MIN_PCT% of those branches' bytes. Both, because
# honest repos share the odd avatar with a leak: measured honest repos held at most 0.3 MiB of
# a denied repo's files, the copies 50 MiB and up. The share spares a project that vendored a
# few listed files. A re-encoded copy has different bytes and is not caught.
COPY_MIN_BYTES=5242880                           # bytes of listed files a copy holds
COPY_MIN_PCT=50                                  # % of the branches' bytes those files make up
